  "caption": "Quinn joined an adult ballet class, added rehearsals and extra practice, and kept a grumbling ankle quiet. Very dancer of Quinn.\n\nMost dance injuries build slowly, often in the feet, ankles, hips and low back, as total load quietly adds up across classes.\n\nWhat can help: strength work off the floor for calves, hips and trunk, tracking all your dance hours, eating enough to fuel training, and mentioning niggles early. Readiness for pointe is best judged by an assessment, not age alone. And no one should force 180° turnout — hip shape varies.\n\nGet it checked if you can't put weight through it, have foot or shin pain at night, or one-sided low back pain that's worse arching back.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
